---
import Highlight from '../components/Highlight.astro';
import SignupForm from '../components/SignupForm.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="The Lazy Horseman · a letter and tools for horse people"
  description="Horses come with a lot of rules nobody can explain, and a lot of jobs nobody should still be doing in a group chat. A weekly letter, and small useful tools for the yard."
  hasLocalSignup
>
  <section class="band hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1><span>Horses are</span><span><Highlight>hard enough.</Highlight></span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">A letter on Thursdays about the things everyone repeats and nobody checks. Software for the jobs your yard still does in a group chat.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <button class="btn btn-lg" type="button" data-signup-target="#signup">Get it Thursday</button>
        <a class="squiggle" href="/tools">See what we are building</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mud" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </section>

  <div class="band marquee" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="marquee-track">
      <span>The hell is a frog anyway? ✦ Rope halters are worth their weight in hay ✦ The benefits of a track system ✦ Your horse is not cold, you are cold ✦ Everything I got wrong about haynets ✦ Nobody knows what "on the bit" means ✦&nbsp;</span>
      <span>The hell is a frog anyway? ✦ Rope halters are worth their weight in hay ✦ The benefits of a track system ✦ Your horse is not cold, you are cold ✦ Everything I got wrong about haynets ✦ Nobody knows what "on the bit" means ✦&nbsp;</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band cream-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">How it goes round here</p>
          <h2>Nobody here is going to tell you your rug is wrong</h2>
          <p>Somebody on your yard has a firm opinion about your rug. Somebody else has one about your feed, and neither of them has read anything.</p>
          <p>Round here nobody minds what you ride or what it cost. The letter goes out on Thursday, the tools are getting built, and that is about the size of it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards">
          <div class="card w1" style="transform:rotate(calc(var(--tilt) * -.6deg))">
            <h3>Mud is the great leveller</h3>
            <p>Every horse in the country is stood in it by November. Whatever the yard cost and whatever the horse cost, somebody is out there at six with a headtorch and a bucket.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card w2" style="transform:rotate(calc(var(--tilt) * .5deg))">
            <h3>Nothing here is for show</h3>
            <p>The headcollar that has lasted nine years cost eleven quid, and nobody has ever advertised it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card w3" style="transform:rotate(calc(var(--tilt) * -.4deg))">
            <h3>Sources at the bottom, always</h3>
            <p>So you can check the working, or print it off and take it to your vet and have an argument with better ammunition than usual.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band makes">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker kicker-green">What comes out of all that</p>
          <h2>A letter, and a bench of tools</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="makes-grid">
        <article class="make w1">
          <p class="make-for">EVERY THURSDAY</p>
          <h3>The letter</h3>
          <p class="make-line">One subject, taken apart properly.</p>
          <p>Hooves one week, haynets the next, and whatever you have all been arguing about at the gate. Five minutes, with the sources underneath.</p>
          <div class="make-go">
            <button class="btn" type="button" data-signup-target="#signup">Get it Thursday</button>
            <a class="squiggle" href="/issues/the-hell-is-a-frog-anyway">Read one first</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="make w2">
          <p class="make-for">BEING BUILT NOW</p>
          <h3>The tools</h3>
          <p class="make-line">For the jobs the yard does the hard way.</p>
          <p>Arena bookings living in a group chat. Track systems drawn on the back of a feed bag. Small, useful software for the bits of keeping horses nobody has got round to fixing.</p>
          <div class="make-go">
            <a class="btn btn-cream" href="/tools">See the tools</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band yard">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="yard-grid">
        <div class="yard-copy">
          <p class="kicker">If you run a yard</p>
          <h2>Nobody has to ask if the school is free at six</h2>
          <p>Facility Booking is the first tool out. Riders see what is open and book it themselves, from their phone or straight from WhatsApp. You decide who gets an account. The group chat goes back to being about lost headcollars.</p>
          <p class="yard-price">Free for one arena, and it stays free.</p>
          <p><a class="squiggle squiggle-ink" href="/tools/facility-booking">See how it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="yard-card">
          <h3>Get in first</h3>
          <p>Leave your email and you will hear the week it opens. No sales call, because there is nobody here to make one.</p>
          <SignupForm
            id="email-yard"
            variant="yard"
            list="yards"
            placeholder="you@youryard.co.uk"
            label="Tell me when it opens"
          />
          <p class="yard-note">FOR YARD OWNERS · SEPARATE FROM THE LETTER</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band signup" id="signup">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Thursday morning, then.</h2>
      <p>One letter a week, five minutes, sources at the bottom. Something to read in the car park while you wait for the rain to go over.</p>
      <SignupForm id="email-main" />
      <p class="fineprint">Free, and one click to leave. No hard feelings either way.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
